[16.015922, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[16.051227, "o", "[\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K  ] M13-01 (13.1) the backend takes the user's identity from the request body, not the signed-in session: anyone can claim to be anyone\r\n[\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K  ] M13-02 (13.1) per-user access is a metadata filter whose value the browser sends (department): a filter is a relevance feature, and a client-supplied scope is a suggestion, not a control\r\n[\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K  ] M13-03 (13.1) implicit metadata filtering is on: a model writes the filter from the user's words, so the user chooses which department's documents come back\r\n[\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K  ] M13-04 (13.1) 2 restricted documents (hr/, it-admin/) sit in a customer-managed knowledge base with no ACL awareness: any caller of Retrieve gets them unless every request carries the right filter\r\n[\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K  ] M13-12 (13.2) write action reset_mfa runs without user confirmation (requireConfirmation is not ENABLED): a retrieved document can trigger it\r\n[\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K  ] M13-13 (13.2) the action Lambda doesn't know who the end user is: it acts on whatever target the model passes, with the agent's own permissions\r\n[\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K  ] M13-14 (13.2) Lambda resource policy lets bedrock.amazonaws.com invoke the function without an AWS:SourceArn condition: any agent (another team's, another account's) can call reset_mfa\r\n[\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K  ] M13-15 (13.2) Lambda execution role allows cognito-idp:* on *: one injected call can do anything the identity service can\r\n[\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K  ] M13-16 (13.2) the agent can run code it doesn't need: the AMAZON.CodeInterpreter action group is enabled\r\n9 \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K, 7 MEDIUM, 1 LOW  (17 findings)\r\n"]
